 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity**: $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels in the chunk, for the population phase. The mask generation is $O(C^2)$ where $C$ is the chunk dimension, due to the 2D iteration over axes. Mesh generation is proportional to the number of exposed faces [S1, unofficial].
--   **Memory Complexity**: $O(C^2)$ for the bitmasks. Specifically, $3 \times C_P^2 \times 8$ bytes for `axis_cols` and `axis_cols_opaque`, and $6 \times C_P^2 \times 8$ bytes for `col_face_masks` [S1, unofficial].
--   **Strengths**: Significantly reduces over-culling in scenes with transparent blocks compared to standard binary greedy meshing. Maintains the performance benefits of bit-parallel operations [S1, unofficial].
--   **Limitations**: Requires a rendering pipeline that supports transparency sorting. Per-face transparency adds complexity and memory overhead [S1, unofficial].
