 -   **When to use**: When rendering voxel worlds with glass, water, or other transparent materials where standard greedy meshing would incorrectly hide visible faces behind transparent blocks [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-This method was developed as an extension to binary greedy meshing to address the limitations of treating all non-air blocks as opaque for culling purposes. It was discussed in the context of the `binary_greedy_mesher_demo` repository, aiming to support transparent voxel textures like glass and opaque blocks with gaps like doors [S1, unofficial]. The technique leverages bitwise operations to efficiently compute face masks that account for transparency, ensuring minimal face count while preserving visual correctness [S1, unofficial].
